# Copy to .env and adjust for your environment. Expo inlines any
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable into the JS bundle at build time — never put
# secrets here (see MOBILE_INTEGRATION_AUDIT.md §38 / §11 / rules 6-7).
#
# Leave unset to fall back to src/config/env.ts's built-in dev/production
# resolution (see mobile/README.md for what that resolves to per platform).

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Android-specific Google OAuth client (see GoogleSignInButton.tsx) — Google
# rejects custom-scheme redirect_uris (gapirai://) for "Web application"
# clients, so Android needs its own "Android" type client registered with
# this package's SHA-1 fingerprint. Without this, the button falls back to
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, which will fail sign-in on Android.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
